{
  "original_id": "newwin-00001-p12",
  "archive_id": "BW2-N01-P12",
  "title": "All partition-restricted counts of nondegenerate 2 by 4 by 3 hypermatrices",
  "batch_label": "新WIN-1批次",
  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "proved",
  "scope": "For every prime power q and every pair of weakly decreasing nonnegative integer triples lambda and mu with mu_j <= lambda_j, lambda_j <= 4-j and mu_j <= 3-j for j=1,2,3, the number of ordered pairs (A,B) of 4-by-3 matrices over F_q with A_rj=0 whenever r>4-lambda_j and B_rj=0 whenever r>4-mu_j, and with nonzero boundary-format hyperdeterminant, is q^9 (q-1)^6 times product_{j=1}^3 [5-j-lambda_j]_q times product_{j=1}^3 [4-j-mu_j]_q, where [r]_q=sum_{a=0}^{r-1} q^a. Nondegeneracy equivalently means rank(sA+tB)=3 for all nonzero (s,t) over the algebraic closure of F_q. All 55 permitted shapes and all prime powers are included. No assertion for k>3 is made.",
  "gate_basis": "Current released terminal, manifest, PDF, TeX freeze, snapshot files, provenance and four audits agree.",
